  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>RWA distributed value fell 5.4% over 30D:</strong> On-chain RWA distributed value at $14.80B (5.4% lower over 30D) hints that tokenized asset growth paused or reversed\u2014more consistent with risk-off allocation or redemptions than a pure news cycle. Related: <a href=\"https://news.google.?oc=5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Why this investment bank expects little demand for tokenized stocks despite SEC\u2019s new trading rules</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Tokenized U.S. Treasuries remain the institutional bridge into RWAs:</strong> adoption is strongest where products plug into cash management, collateral, and liquidity workflows. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/ondo-lets-institutions-convert-stocks-directly-into-tokenized-shares?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ondo lets institutions convert stocks directly into tokenized shares</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li><li><strong>Tokenized T-bill supply is still expanding through new products:</strong> That usually shows up first as new issuer and product supply, then as higher distributed value and denser collateral-style use across networks and platforms. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/09/21/why-this-investment-bank-sees-little-demand-for-tokenized-stocks-despite-sec-s-new-trading-rules\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Why this investment bank expects little demand for tokenized stocks despite SEC\u2019s new trading rules</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Regulatory framing still decides product access:</strong> Clearer rules tend to unlock balance-sheet participation and collateral workflows even when aggregate on-chain totals reprice slowly. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/09/22/next-for-the-u-s-sec-agency-s-chief-crypto-counsel-illuminates-path-for-custody\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Next for the U.S. SEC: Agency&#x27;s chief crypto counsel illuminates path for custody</a> (CoinDesk).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
